  "question": {
    "text": "Two straignt conducting plates form an angle $\\theta$ where their ends are joined. A conducting bar in contact with the plates and forming an isosceles triangle with them starts at the vertex at time $t=0$ and moves with constant velocity $\\vec{v}$ to the right as shown in figure. A magnetic field $\\vec{B}$ points out of the page. The magnitude of emf induced at $t=1$ second will be\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/JcdWGfhkzs0qGv95r8EH5pC0p1muE6-gjmsqQaWp3Ns.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
